<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lex Hortensia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">287 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lex Hortensia was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> of 287 BCE, passed under the dictator Quintus Hortensius after a secession of the plebeians. It made the resolutions of the plebeian assembly binding on all Roman citizens, patricians included. It is traditionally regarded as the end of the Conflict of the Orders between patricians and plebeians.</p></div>
